Package: robotcompR
Title: Robotics, Kinematics, Dynamics, and Motion Planning
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Tools for robot modeling, kinematics, dynamics, collision
    checking, motion planning, trajectory generation and mobile robotics.
    It provides spatial mathematics on the rotation and rigid motion groups
    SO(2), SO(3), SE(2) and SE(3) (rotation matrices, Euler angles,
    axis-angle, unit quaternions, exponential and logarithm maps and their
    Jacobians) following Sola, Deray and Atchuthan (2018)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.1812.01537>; rigid-body tree models with revolute,
    continuous, prismatic and fixed joints, Denavit-Hartenberg parameters
    and import and export of the Unified Robot Description Format ('URDF');
    forward kinematics, geometric and analytic Jacobians, manipulability and
    numerical inverse kinematics with joint limits; recursive Newton-Euler,
    composite rigid body and articulated body dynamics following
    Featherstone (2008) <doi:10.1007/978-1-4899-7560-7>, with torque-driven
    simulation; convex collision geometry with the Gilbert-Johnson-Keerthi
    (GJK) distance algorithm of Gilbert, Johnson and Keerthi (1988)
    <doi:10.1109/56.2083>, the expanding polytope algorithm (EPA) for
    penetration depth and continuous collision checking by conservative
    advancement; sampling-based motion planning with rapidly exploring
    random trees (RRT), RRT-Connect of Kuffner and LaValle (2000)
    <doi:10.1109/ROBOT.2000.844730>, RRT* of Karaman and Frazzoli (2011)
    <doi:10.1177/0278364911406761> and probabilistic roadmaps (PRM) of
    Kavraki et al. (1996) <doi:10.1109/70.508439>; polynomial, trapezoidal
    and Cartesian trajectories; unicycle, differential-drive and bicycle
    mobile robots with path following; localization with extended and
    unscented Kalman filters (EKF, UKF) and particle filters; occupancy grid
    mapping, simultaneous localization and mapping with an extended Kalman
    filter (EKF-SLAM) and SE(2) and SE(3) pose graph optimization. No
    'MATLAB', 'Python' or 'ROS 2' installation is needed. The package is
    intended for research and education and is not certified for
    controlling physical hardware.
